":"COVID-19. However, few broad-spectrum antiviral drugs have been evaluated against ","x":7.8,"y":130.43,"size":10.0},{"text":"COVID-19 in clinical trials, resulted in clinical recovery.  ","x":7.8,"y":143.02,"size":10.0},{"text":"     In the current review, we summarize and comparatively analyze the emergence and ","x":7.8,"y":155.62,"size":10.0},{"text":"pathogenicity of COVID-19 infection and previous human coronaviruses severe acute ","x":7.8,"y":168.43,"size":10.0},{"text":"respiratory syndrome coronavirus (SARS-CoV) and middle east","x":7.8,"y":181.02,"size":10.0},{"text":"respiratory syndrome ","x":329.09,"y":181.02,"size":10.0},{"text":"coronavirus (MERS-CoV). We also discuss the approaches for developing effective ","x":7.8,"y":193.65,"size":10.0},{"text":"vaccines and therapeutic combinations to cope with this ","x":7.8,"y":206.45,"size":10.0},{"text":"viral outbreak.  ","x":288.9,"y":206.45,"size":10.0}],"text":"Abstract  The coronavirus disease 19 (COVID -19) is a highly transmittable and pathogenic  viral infection caused by severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV- 2), which emerged in Wuhan, China and spread  around the world. Genomic analysis  revealed that  SARS-CoV-2 is phylogenetically related to severe acute respiratory  syndrome -like (SARS-like) bat viruses, therefore bats could be the possible primary  reservoir. The  intermediate source of origin and transfer to humans is not known,  however,  the rapid human to human transfer has been confirmed widely.  There is no clinically approved antiviral drug or vaccine available to be used against  COVID-19. However, few broad-spectrum antiviral drugs have been evaluated against  COVID-19 in clinical trials, resulted in clinical recovery.        In the current review, we summarize and comparatively analyze the emergence and  pathogenicity of COVID-19 infection and previous human coronaviruses severe acute  respiratory syndrome coronavirus (SARS-CoV) and middle east respiratory syndrome  coronavirus (MERS-CoV). We also discuss the approaches for developing effective  vaccines and therapeutic combinations to cope with this  viral outbreak.  ","page":10},"5a0c999897bbfad2fd14":{"type":"paragraph","page":11,"text":"Activity #3: Bawal Judgmental","bbox":[71.82499694824219,72.0579833984375,326.8199768066406,84.89498138427734]}},"excerptBlocks":{"concepts:0":["7f493720c7e9a14ead3c","52cd0827c352eaa232c6","9ff5a7ca6121293836e9","801e35d1bf28cb3cbd1e"],"concepts:1":["407c7681807b607acf6b","833171fd1cca274a5416","27f48b032067aeecee8f"],"concepts:2":["5a0c999897bbfad2fd14"]},"games":[{"difficulty":"easy","answer":"CLAIM OF FACT","explanation":"CLAIM OF FACT A claim whether something is true or untrue but there must always be potential for controversy, conflict and change.","timeLimitSeconds":45,"source":{"fileId":"1RiUzPjHIyUjn-H1UFej_TbfzAWUI8wAD","page":8,"quote":"CLAIM OF FACT A claim whether something is true or untrue but there must always be potential for controversy, conflict and change.","answerQuote":"CLAIM OF FACT","sourceId":"8a1b514c1ef6beb3","kind":"definition-recall"},"id":"g10-q2-m5-type-8a1b514c1ef6beb3","type":"typeHunter","prompt":"Type the PDF term that completes this source statement.","contextSentence":"____ A claim whether something is true or untrue but there must always be potential for controversy, conflict and change."}],"assets":{"/assets/curriculum/figures/7e6c7beee1c903a4da0a2693.webp":"data:image/webp;base64,","/assets/curriculum/figures/2d6348d38e7608759e7cc9ba.webp":"data:image/webp;base64,"},"sourceSections":[{"id":"concepts","title":"Concepts & Rules","kind":"discussion","entries":[{"page":9,"blockIds":["7f493720c7e9a14ead3c","52cd0827c352eaa232c6","9ff5a7ca6121293836e9","801e35d1bf28cb3cbd1e"]},{"page":10,"blockIds":["407c7681807b607acf6b","833171fd1cca274a5416","27f48b032067aeecee8f"]},{"page":11,"blockIds":["5a0c999897bbfad2fd14"]}]}]}
